                 README: Motorola MVME162 (mv162)

This file contains board-specific information for the Motorola MVME162,
MVME162FX, and the Motorola MVME162LX target boards.  
Specifically, this file contains information on any BSP interface changes 
from previous software or hardware versions, and contains caveats that the 
user must be aware of before using this BSP.  Additionally, the target board's 
manual page entry (i.e., man mv162) provides board-specific information 
necessary to run VxWorks, and should be read before this BSP is used.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

RELEASE 1.0/0 of MVME162LX and 1.0/2 of MVME162

    This BSP supports all the MVME162 boards (MVME162, MVME162FX, and 
    MVME162LX).  Although the default configuration will run on all the
    target boards, only two serial ports will be available on the MVME162LX.

    To properly configure the MVME162LX's four on-board serial I/O channels, 
    the MVME162LX pre-processor directive must be defined in config.h.
    Simply change the #if statement above the MVME162LX macro to TRUE,
    then re-build the VxWorks image.

    Due to the snooping problems with the Test And Set (TAS) command over the 
    VME, the shared memory pool for the backplane driver is defined in the low
    memory and marked as non-cacheable. Bus snooping the VME accesses has been 
    turned off due to this problem. This will not effect the cache and snooping
    for the on-board devices such as ethernet and SCSI as snooping will be 
    turned on for these devices. Memory from 0x2000 to 0x20000 has been 
    allocated for shared memory. The RAM_LOW_ADRS for this reason has been 
    raised from 0x1000 to 0x20000. These changes would be in effect until 
    the snooping problems with TAS instruction are fixed on the hardware.
    For more information read target.nr.

